      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T07:59:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The printk message from panic_bad_stack() is helpful in analyzing bad_stack issues.\nHowever, it often does not appear in the kernel log, so I would like to get help with this hook.\nThis usually happens when an exception occurs during printk() processing, which may be a hardware malfunction.",
      "parentUuid": "66ff1370_6b3a725c",
      "revId": "79e067b73aaea95d7725fc55360d4a26cb50f269",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45068be4_70d28c22",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T17:56:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is a hardware malfunction that leads to lost kernel messages during handling of bad_stack really such a common occurrence that it requires this kind of kernel change to make ramdump debugging easier? This seems like it would be a very rare case so this change is really not very useful.",
      "parentUuid": "3f09bad5_ba7a6dc1",
      "revId": "79e067b73aaea95d7725fc55360d4a26cb50f269",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bcb5c6b_50866341",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1895335
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-24T00:03:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Although the problem may be rare, it doesn’t mean we can ignore it. In production, we must address even these rare issues. This patch is one of the solutions we’ve successfully used in manufacturing. I hope you understand.",
      "parentUuid": "45068be4_70d28c22",
      "revId": "79e067b73aaea95d7725fc55360d4a26cb50f269",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd58d5c2_71da95f0",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-24T17:56:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is exactly what I\u0027m afraid of. These patches make me think there are 100s more patches like this coming to provide extra information about many other uncommon issues. Why does this rare case need a special hook but some other failure in sched or mm  (that is possible but unlikely) doesn\u0027t need a hook like this? How are you deciding which rare events are worthy of all this extra effort? We can\u0027t accept 100s of hooks for this kind of offline event analysis. What is so special about this particular case? (and the other similar cases in this patch series)\n\nPlease convince me that these 4 patches are not the beginning of a storm of patches to add hooks purely for the benefit of bootloader crash triage capabilities.",
      "parentUuid": "9bcb5c6b_50866341",
      "revId": "79e067b73aaea95d7725fc55360d4a26cb50f269",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9137c51c_f34d133b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1982050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-25T02:04:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These problems occur as a result of watchdog resets and do not leave direct clues in the kernel logs.\nWe need to first identify which device driver is causing the problem or what task is causing it, then we can perform a practical analysis for resolving the issue.\nWe don\u0027t have much time to spend on initial analysis.\n\nThese patches are codes for problems that we have met repeatedly over the years while working on many projects.\nI don\u0027t think they suddenly increased to dozens.",
      "parentUuid": "bd58d5c2_71da95f0",
      "revId": "79e067b73aaea95d7725fc55360d4a26cb50f269",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77923236_0225ce02",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1982050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-25T09:20:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And in the case of the current patch, I will consider whether we can use `trace_android_rvh_handle_bad_stack` instead of adding a new hook to `panic_bad_stack()`.",
      "parentUuid": "9137c51c_f34d133b",
      "revId": "79e067b73aaea95d7725fc55360d4a26cb50f269",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
